Spec: Isolated Android native gateway verification

Purpose:
  Verify Keystore, Binder UID and private stream behavior on an explicitly owned headless emulator.

Structure:
  ./EmulatorHarness: Kernel-owned emulator and isolated ADB server lifetime.
  ./NativeHarness: Windows publisher and independent Android SDK acceptance orchestration.

Owns:
  ./README.md
  ./verify.ps1

Must:
  Use an isolated ADB port with physical USB discovery disabled and explicit emulator serial for every device command.
  Verify the guest emulator and architecture before installing test packages.
  Keep emulator results distinct from ARM64 phone and real-network acceptance.
  Allow an explicit generated runtime and authenticated backend fixture selection for native FRP verification while preserving the default direct-preview acceptance path.

  Freeze the hashes of all four built APKs before installation in a unique run manifest, then attach that exact manifest to the acceptance summary; later builds cannot substitute their artifacts for tested binaries.
